course: dictionary
lesson: 9818
title: Swedish: a word with two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Swedish has two main meanings. As an adjective, it tells you that something comes from Sweden, as in «Swedish food» or «a Swedish girl». As a noun, it names the language spoken in Sweden.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is being used. In «She speaks Swedish at home with her grandmother», Swedish is a language, because you speak a language. In «a Swedish girl», Swedish describes the girl and tells you where she is from.
explain: Look at this sentence: «Young people such as Greta Thunberg, a Swedish girl who missed school on Fridays to protest, have spoken up about the environment.» Swedish sits in front of girl, so it describes her. It tells you Greta is from Sweden.
fact: Swedish begins with a capital letter, like other words for countries and their people, such as English and French.
fact: Sweden is a country in northern Europe, and its capital city is Stockholm.
fact: «Swedish» means from or to do with Sweden, as in «Swedish meatballs».
fact: Swedish is the language spoken in Sweden, and partly in Finland.
fact: Swedish is related to English, Danish and Norwegian, so some of its words look a little like English words.
exercise: «She cooked Swedish meatballs for the whole class.» What does Swedish tell us about the meatballs? | They are very spicy | They came from the shop | *They come from Sweden | They are made of fish from Finland
exercise: «In Sweden, children learn Swedish at school.» What does Swedish mean here? | A country in northern Europe | *The language spoken in Sweden | A girl from Sweden | A kind of furniture
exercise: Which city is the capital of Sweden? | Oslo | Helsinki | *Stockholm | Gothenburg
test: «Ella is learning Swedish this year.» What does Swedish mean? | *The language of Sweden | A Scottish word | A kind of furniture | A person from Sweden
test: «The Swedish team won the match.» What kind of word is Swedish here? | *An adjective, it tells us which team | A place name, like London | A verb, it means to win | A noun, it names a language
exam: In «a Swedish girl who missed school on Fridays to protest», what does Swedish tell us about the girl? | She is a famous author | She is from Norway | She speaks only English | *She is from Sweden
